<div id="recipe-82304-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-82304-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="82304" data-servings="10"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Ingredients</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="0"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac34;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">warm water</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">at 110 &deg;F degrees</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">honey</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="2"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1 &frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">instant yeast</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">aka quick rise yeast &ndash; (5g)</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="3"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">extra virgin olive oil</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">whole milk</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">at room temperature</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3 &frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cups</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">all purpose flour</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">plus more for rolling (423 g)</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1 &frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">8g</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-unit-conversion-container wprm-unit-conversion-container-82304 wprm-unit-conversion-container-links wprm-block-text-normal" style=""><a href="#" role="button" class="wprm-unit-conversion wprmpuc-active" data-system="1" data-recipe="82304" style="" aria-label="Change unit system to US Customary">US Customary</a> &ndash; <a href="#" role="button" class="wprm-unit-conversion" data-system="2" data-recipe="82304" style="" aria-label="Change unit system to Metric">Metric</a></div></div>
<div id="recipe-82304-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82304-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82304"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place &frac34; cup of warm water and 1 teaspoon of honey in a measuring cup. Stir to ensure that the honey is fully dissolved.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="The yeast activated and mixed with olive oil in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Easy-lavash-bread-recipe.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the yeast and stir until it is well combined. Let it rest for 5 minutes. It will have a thick layer of bubbles on top.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">In the same measuring cup, add &frac14; cup olive oil and &frac12; cup milk. Give it a good stir. Set it aside.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Combine 3 &frac14; cups all-purpose flour and 1 &frac14; teaspoons kosher salt in a large bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Dry ingredients are being mixed with the wet to make lavash dough." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Homemade-lavash-bread.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Add the yeast mixture and knead for 5 minutes, first mixing the dough until no flour remains and then turning it into a ball. In the end, it will be a very sticky dough, and that is normal.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Cover the dough with a clean kitchen towel and let it rest in a warm part of your kitchen for 20 minutes. It will get slightly larger in size.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="The dough is placed in a bowl to rise and a person is kneading it." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Lavash.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer the now-rested dough to a lightly floured surface.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To knead the dough, press it with the heel of your hand, then push it away, fold it back over, and rotate it 45 degrees. Repeat this process for 5 minutes or until the dough is smooth. If it&rsquo;s too sticky to work with, sprinkle in a bit more flour, 1 tablespoon at a time.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-8" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Shape the dough into a log and divide it into 10 equal pieces.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="The dough is cut into smaller pieces." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Middle-Eastern-flatbread.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-9" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Roll each piece into a ball, dust it with flour, and transfer it onto a plate. Loosely cover the plate with a kitchen towel and let it rest for 20 minutes.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-10" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When you&rsquo;re ready to cook, heat a large (12-inch) nonstick or cast-iron skillet over high heat for 5 minutes. The pan needs to be very hot to keep the dough from sticking. To test, flick a few drops of water into the skillet. If they sizzle and disappear right away, it&rsquo;s ready.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-11" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">While the pan heats up, roll out one dough ball into a 10-inch circle using a rolling pin and more flour as needed. As you roll, it might be tricky to keep a perfect circle, and that&rsquo;s totally fine. Just do your best.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Lavash dough rolled out with a rolling pin." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lavash-flatbread.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-12" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Carefully transfer the rolled dough to the hot skillet. Cook for 10 seconds (you&rsquo;ll see bubbles forming), then flip. Cook for another 10 seconds, then flip again. Repeat for a total of 3-4 flips or until it looks fully cooked and has golden spots.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Lavash cooked in a skillet from the top view." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-bread-lavash.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-13" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">As soon as it&rsquo;s done, wrap the warm lavash in a clean kitchen towel and place it in a basket to keep warm. Continue adding each cooked piece to the basket, keeping them wrapped so they stay soft and warm while you finish the rest.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82304-step-0-14" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Repeat the same rolling and cooking process with the remaining dough balls.</div></li></ul></div></div>
